% Test cases for the heating pads policy (heating_pads.le): synthetic claims,
% one per criterion of LCD L33784 and per code the LCD or Policy Article
% A52502 denies. The finding is recorded as the treating practitioner's, a
% medical reviewer's or the Council's; a finding nobody made leaves the
% answer conditional. A heating pad is a purchase: no rental month.

the target language is: prolog.

the knowledge base heating_pads cases includes these resources:
    heating_pads.

the knowledge base heating_pads cases includes:

query pay is:
    which claim is payable.

query rn is:
    which claim is reasonable and necessary.

query stage is:
    the query fails at which section.

query flip is:
    which minimal change to the scenario makes it the case that
        claim 1 is payable.

% A complete claim for a standard electric heating pad (E0210) for
% osteoarthritic joint stiffness: the finding, the standard written order
% communicated before the date of service, the delivery and its proof.
scenario standard_pad_complete is:
    claim 1 is for the heating pad.
    the HCPCS code of the heating pad is "E0210".
    the heating pad is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding heating pad indicated about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "to decrease joint stiffness from osteoarthritis of the knees".
    the order for the heating pad is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the heating pad is signed by the treating practitioner.
    the order for the heating pad includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the heating pad includes order date.
    the order for the heating pad includes description of the item.
    the order for the heating pad includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the heating pad includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the heating pad was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the heating pad was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the heating pad.
    pay expects answers ["claim 1 is payable"].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers [].

% The purpose is not decided: nothing in the record says what the pad is
% for, so the answer is conditional on the finding.
scenario purpose_not_decided is:
    claim 1 is for the heating pad.
    the HCPCS code of the heating pad is "E0210".
    the heating pad is furnished to Ben.
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"] and unknowns ["the finding heating pad indicated about Ben is established"].

% The exclusion: the pad is provided to treat pain due to diabetic
% neuropathy — not reasonable and necessary whatever the finding.
scenario peripheral_neuropathy is:
    claim 1 is for the heating pad.
    the HCPCS code of the heating pad is "E0210".
    the heating pad is furnished to Cy.
    the residence of Cy is private residence.
    the finding heating pad indicated about Cy is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "to relieve burning foot pain".
    the heating pad is provided to treat pain due to peripheral neuropathy.
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at question"].

% The Council finds the record shows no covered purpose: the note names no
% pain, stiffness, muscle or inflammatory condition the pad would treat.
scenario purpose_unsupported_council is:
    claim 1 is for the heating pad.
    the HCPCS code of the heating pad is "E0210".
    the heating pad is furnished to Dee.
    the finding heating pad indicated about Dee is unsupported, according to the Council, because "the treating practitioner's note states only that the beneficiary requested a heating pad and names no pain, stiffness, muscle spasm or inflammation it would treat".
    rn expects answers [].

% A moist electric heating pad (E0215) and a water circulating heat pad
% with pump (E0217): denied as not reasonable and necessary, whatever the
% finding.
scenario moist_and_water_circulating is:
    claim 1 is for the moist pad.
    the HCPCS code of the moist pad is "E0215".
    the moist pad is furnished to Eve.
    claim 2 is for the water pad.
    the HCPCS code of the water pad is "E0217".
    the water pad is furnished to Eve.
    the finding heating pad indicated about Eve is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "to relax paraspinal muscle spasm".
    rn expects answers [].

% A replacement pump (E0236) for a water circulating system, and a heat lamp
% (E0205): denied as not reasonable and necessary.
scenario pump_and_heat_lamp is:
    claim 1 is for the pump.
    the HCPCS code of the pump is "E0236".
    the pump is furnished to Fay.
    claim 2 is for the heat lamp.
    the HCPCS code of the heat lamp is "E0205".
    the heat lamp is furnished to Fay.
    the finding heating pad indicated about Fay is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "to reduce inflammation of the shoulder".
    rn expects answers [].

% A hydrocollator unit (E0239): in scope, but institutional equipment
% outside the benefit — the claim fails at applicability.
scenario hydrocollator is:
    claim 1 is for the hydrocollator.
    the HCPCS code of the hydrocollator is "E0239".
    the hydrocollator is furnished to Gus.
    the residence of Gus is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers [].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at applicability"].

% Reasonable and necessary, but the order is not signed by the treating
% practitioner: payable fails at the remedy; the signature flips it.
scenario order_unsigned is:
    claim 1 is for the heating pad.
    the HCPCS code of the heating pad is "E0210".
    the heating pad is furnished to Ann.
    the residence of Ann is private residence.
    the date of service of claim 1 is 2026-03-01.
    the finding heating pad indicated about Ann is established, according to the treating practitioner, because "to decrease joint stiffness from osteoarthritis of the knees".
    the order for the heating pad is dated 2026-02-20.
    the order for the heating pad includes beneficiary name.
    the order for the heating pad includes order date.
    the order for the heating pad includes description of the item.
    the order for the heating pad includes quantity to be dispensed.
    the order for the heating pad includes treating practitioner name.
    the order for the heating pad was communicated to the supplier on 2026-02-22.
    the heating pad was delivered on 2026-03-01.
    the supplier holds proof of delivery for the heating pad.
    pay expects answers [].
    rn expects answers ["claim 1 is reasonable and necessary"].
    stage expects answers ["the query fails at remedy"].
    flip expects changes [["add: the order for the heating pad is signed by the treating practitioner"]].
